      "content": "I am currently reviewing some data for a paper on morphophonemic allomorphy in agglutinative systems. I'm particularly interested in how small, discrete functional units—morphemes—interact with the root to trigger specific phonological shifts.\n\nCan you provide a formal, structural breakdown for the following Finnish words? I need to see the exact boundaries between the root and the various suffixes, and I want a precise explanation of how the \"internal\" parts of the word change when these small functional units are attached.\n\n1. jalka -> jaloissa (in the feet)\n2. kivi -> kivien (of the stones)\n3. vesi -> vedessä (in the water)\n\nPlease focus on the shifting behavior of the stems and the specific rules governing these transformations.",
